---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../site';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<PageLayout
  title="About"
  description="What pulse360 is, how our news briefs are produced, and who to contact."
  updated="October 16, 2026"
>
  <p>
    pulse360 is an independent news digest. We follow reporting from established
    outlets around the world, including wire services, public broadcasters and
    specialist publications, and turn it into short, plain-language briefs that you
    can read in a minute or two.
  </p>
  <p>
    We don't claim to replace original journalism. Every brief names and links to
    the outlets that did the reporting, and we encourage you to read them.
  </p>

  <h2>How a brief is made</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Monitoring.</strong> Every few hours we check a fixed list of news
      sources, from Reuters, AP and the BBC to sector publications in technology,
      business, sport and entertainment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Grouping.</strong> When several outlets report the same event, we group
      their coverage into one story rather than publishing it several times.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Selection.</strong> Stories are ranked by how widely they are covered,
      how credible the reporting outlets are and how significant the subject is. We
      skip stories when the available reporting is too thin to summarize accurately.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Drafting with AI.</strong> An AI language model drafts the brief, under
      strict instructions to use only facts stated by the reporting outlets, to
      attribute claims, and never to add speculation or invented detail.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sourcing and corrections.</strong> Each brief lists its sources. If you
      find an error, tell us and we will correct it. See our
      <a href={`${base}editorial-policy`}>editorial policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What we add</h2>
  <p>
    Beyond the briefs themselves, pulse360 tags every story by country, topic and
    tone, so you can see at a glance what is happening in a particular
    <a href={`${base}country`}>country</a> or field, and how coverage compares across
    outlets.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, corrections or feedback: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    More options are on our <a href={`${base}contact`}>contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
